WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.659
If you want to hear the unknown truth about
where Gordon went in all that time between

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:04.880
Saw and Saw 7

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.460
(yeah, I prefer to call it Saw
7 instead of Saw 3D, so get used to it)

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.820
then stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.600
Jigsaw, the man who brought his judgement
down upon the world of the Saw franchise had

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.420
many disciples who lent him a helping hand
at some point along his journey, but the man

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.380
considered to be his greatest asset was
Dr. Lawrence Gordon.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.390
Welcome to Horror History.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.410
My name is the emo version of Kevin from Home
Alone…

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.380
I actually used to get that a lot when I was
a kid… minus the emo part…

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.100
Today we’re covering a fan favorite.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.730
It’s Dr. Lawrence Gordon.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.690
Gordon was played by actor Cary Elwes, who
appears in the original Saw, and comes back

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:40.790
for Saw 7.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:44.770
After a financial contract dispute hobbled
the original plans for Gordon to appear in

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.400
Saw III, pun intended, Elwes had to wait for
a higher budget before making his return.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.399
But Elwes, much like his character, continued
to keep tabs on the Saw world without making

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:54.920
an appearance for years before his triumphant
comeback.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.380
We’re gonna analyse Dr. Gordon’s entire
life, so let’s take it back to the start

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.160
of his story.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:08.920
Lawrence Gordon graduated from Indiana University’s
School of Medicine on June 4th, 1979.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.420
This was the first major accomplishment he
would achieve in his impressive medical career.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.960
He would become a doctor, surgeon, and later
oncologist at the Angel of Mercy Hospital.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:21.689
He married a woman named Alison, and in 1996
they gave birth to their only daughter, Diana.

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:25.709
Lawrence and Alison did discuss having another
child after Diana, but ultimately decided

00:01:25.709 --> 00:01:29.600
their schedules were too busy, and they barely
had time to concentrate on the daughter they

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.100
had.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.139
The busy schedules put a strain on their relationship,
and Dr. Gordon became cold and emotionless

00:01:34.139 --> 00:01:36.930
towards his wife as she became pissy and unruly
towards him.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.719
His constant preoccupation with work also
caused his daughter to feel ire towards his

00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:43.570
pager and she felt that work got in between
her and her father.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.569
In 2004, Dr. Gordon’s relationship with
his wife was very weak and he’s having an

00:01:47.569 --> 00:01:50.569
affair with a medical student at the hospital
named Carla Song.

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:53.380
They would arrange times to meet at seedy
hotel rooms in the middle of the middle of

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:53.880
the night.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.500
In June of 2003, Dr. Lynn Denlon was working
under Dr. Gordon in the oncology department

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:02.200
where they diagnosed a colon cancer patient
named John Kramer with an Inoperable Frontal

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.640
Lobe Tumor or Glioblastoma Mulitforme.

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.700
Nine months after that, on March 24th, 2004
he was found to have speech altering brain

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.520
damage due to more cancerous growths.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.219
When Dr. Gordon called John into his office
to tell him how long he had to live, John

00:02:14.219 --> 00:02:15.879
found his demeanor to be cold and harsh.

00:02:15.879 --> 00:02:19.730
John felt that he did not cherish life, and
did not appreciate the effects that telling

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:22.310
a man his expiration date would have psychologically.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.170
John planned to rehabilitate the doctor using
an elaborate game that Lawrence would be forced

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.170
to partake in.

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.659
John would soon become known as “The Jigsaw
Killer” for the trademark Jigsaw piece he

00:02:30.659 --> 00:02:32.099
cut out of each of his victims.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:35.340
In May of 2004 Gordon would learn of Jigsaw
for the first time.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.930
He was out late one night seeing Carla, and
the next day while examining John’s tumor

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:42.739
for an audience of Carla and the other students,
he’s called out for his emotionless medical

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:44.780
proceedings by an orderly named Zep.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.830
Lawrence mocks Zep for having “special bonds
with the patients.”

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:51.060
Before he can get back to his demonstration,
he’s called into his office for another

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:51.840
distraction.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:55.980
There, he meets two cops, Sing and Tapp, who
question him about his whereabouts the night before.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.420
Gordon’s pen light was found at the crime
scene of one of Jigsaw’s victims where a

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:02.700
man had been burned to death, so the cops
wanted him to provide an alibi.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.379
Not wanting to admit he had cheated on his
wife, Gordon is hesitant to provide his whereabouts

00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:07.870
and they take him down to the station.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.680
His lawyer and friend, Brett, recommends that
Gordon give his alibi while he still has a

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.459
chance, and in doing so, they’re able to
clear his name, but one of the detectives,

00:03:14.459 --> 00:03:16.000
David Tapp, is still suspicious.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.270
They ask Gordon to stay a bit longer to hear
the testimony of one Jigsaw victim that escaped

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:24.209
her trap, so he sticks around to hear the
story of Amanda Young and is horrified by

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:27.739
the brutality, but still has no answers as
to why his pen light was found.

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:31.531
Merely knowing about Jigsaw was not enough
to get Gordon to change his ways though, because

00:03:31.531 --> 00:03:35.430
five months later, in October, he’s up late
working once again when his daughter Diana

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:38.200
has a little sleepwalking incident and asks
to see her Dad.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.420
He doesn’t even look up from his computer
as his wife tells him about what happened.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.160
I imagine this is what I look like when I’m
editing a video.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:47.359
He does eventually go to put her to bed and
check the room with her because she believes

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:48.450
there’s a man in there.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.459
“There’s no such thing as the bad man.

00:03:50.459 --> 00:03:51.980
Now can you go to sleep?”

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.459
I would beg to differ, but it’s Lawrence
doesn’t notice anyone in the room, and eventually

00:03:55.459 --> 00:03:58.109
gets called away when Carla tries to contact
him using his pager.

00:03:58.109 --> 00:04:01.530
On his way out, his wife tries to pick a fight
with him, because she’s completely starved

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:03.129
for passion in the relationship.

00:04:03.129 --> 00:04:07.040
He meets Carla at a run down joint known as
The Hotel Barfly, but instead of hooking up,

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.609
his better judgement kicks in and he tells
her they should stop.

00:04:09.609 --> 00:04:12.799
This could be because he actually felt bad
about his actions, but I think it may have

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:16.569
had more to do with that fact that Carla crossed
a line by buzzing his pager while he was at

00:04:16.569 --> 00:04:17.160
home.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:22.040
“Why did you deem it necessary to page me
when you knew I was at home?

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.360
You can’t do that.”

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:26.789
Before leaving, a call comes in, which alarms
him because nobody is supposed to know their

00:04:26.789 --> 00:04:27.500
location.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:28.980
On the other end a voice tells him,

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.639
“I know what you’re doing...”

00:04:30.639 --> 00:04:34.720
The voice is raspy and whispered, but it doesn’t
sound like the voice that Jigsaw usually uses

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:35.889
to address his victims.

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:37.770
“I want to play a game.”

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.530
I think this may actually be Zep, who was
also a part of Jigsaw’s game and had to

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:43.660
follow his instructions if he wanted to survive.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:47.590
Dr. Gordon hurried home after this, not realizing
that he was being followed by a photographer

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:51.470
named Adam Stanheight, who had been hired
by a still suspicious Detective Tapp to keep

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.470
an eye on him.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.669
Adam would leave, however, before seeing the
ambush that would take place shortly after

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.020
in the parking garage.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:16.420
Doctor Gordon woke up in a dark, dilapidated
bathroom with his ankle chained to an immovable

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:16.920
pipe.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.040
Across the room, Adam was in a similar predicament,
but Lawrence did not yet know who Adam was.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:25.280
There is another man in the center of the
room, who is pretending KEY WORD: PRETENDING

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.389
to be dead, and this is John Kramer.

00:05:27.389 --> 00:05:31.180
Gordon turns on the light and realizes that
everything in the room is old and rusting

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.840
other than the clock, which is new.

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:35.620
He finds a tape in his pocket, along with
a bullet and a key.

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:37.830
He throws his tape to Adam for him to play
it out loud.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.699
It’s a voice recording by Jigsaw, telling
Gordon that he’s getting a wake up call.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:42.849
Roll the tape.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.780
“Every day of your working life you have
given people the news that they’re gonna

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.300
die soon.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.860
Now you will be the cause of death.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:57.460
Your aim in this game is to kill Adam.”

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.730
Jigsaw tells him he has to kill Adam by 6
and gives him two clues: the red substance on

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:05.240
the ground is actually laced with poison and
X marks the spot.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.940
He also says that Alison and Diana’s lives
are at stake at well, and a whisper at the

00:06:08.949 --> 00:06:10.300
end: follow your heart.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.860
Gordon notices the heart on the toilet, which
leads to Adam finding the hacksaws in there,

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.479
but they aren’t strong enough to cut the
chains.

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:18.880
That’s when Dr. Gordon realizes their purpose
is to cut off their feet.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:22.340
He remembers about Amanda, and how Jigsaw
was still on the loose after that.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.820
They discover a camera is watching them behind
the mirror, and Gordon begins to think more

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:29.240
creatively about how to overcome the game
by likening it to his work.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:32.510
“To overcome something you have to understand
what a perfect engine it is.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.460
That’s how you fight disease.”

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.560
This line shows John Kramer why Lawrence is
actually a perfect candidate to win the game

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.940
and become his successor.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:43.389
Gordon doesn’t have the engineering know-how
that Kramer does, but he shows an ability

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:47.990
to use concepts in what he does know, medicine,
to accomplish whatever he puts his mind to.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:51.800
But Gordon would have to be pushed to his
limit before having the opportunity to prove

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:52.460
his worth.

00:06:52.460 --> 00:06:55.680
While reflecting on the last words he said
to his daughter, he shows Adam a picture of

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:59.260
her from his wallet, and Adam finds a clue
that leads him to ask Gordon to try turning

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.260
out the lights.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:04.220
Glow in the dark paint illuminates the X,
and Gordon smashes through to find a box containing

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.900
a phone and two cigarettes.

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:09.830
Gordon is suspicious about how Adam knew to
turn off the lights, and Adam eventually reveals

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.960
that he was hiding a note found in the wallet
on the back of a picture of Alison and Diana

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.250
being held captive.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:17.960
Upon seeing this photo, Gordon emotionally
breaks down.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:20.300
“WHAT DID YOU DO TO THEM YOU BASTARD?”

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.120
But hold on… is Gordon really losing his
cool right here?

00:07:23.129 --> 00:07:24.449
I think maybe not.

00:07:24.449 --> 00:07:28.110
See, Gordon already knew that his family was
in danger, plus he’s never demonstrated

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:32.830
anything other being cool, collected and calculating
when faced with any kind of adversity; whether

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.900
it be his unstable wife, being accused of
commiting a crime or finding himself in a

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.720
life or death stakes escape room.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.759
Then take his next move into account.

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:44.620
He devises a plan where he pretends to kill
Adam by whispering to him to play dead while

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:47.960
the lights are off and making it look like
he tossed the cigarette dipped in poison rather

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:48.979
than the clean one.

00:07:48.979 --> 00:07:52.509
With this plan in mind, it makes sense that
Dr. Gordon would want to sell the performance

00:07:52.509 --> 00:07:55.960
by pretending to have a meltdown over this
photo, making it look like there was a valid

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.160
reason that he now decided to kill Adam.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.020
This level of thoroughness is another great
example of why Lawrence possesses the material

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.280
needed to be Jigsaw.

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:07.849
Unfortunately for Dr. Gordon, Adam’s acting
is not quite as on point as his own.

00:08:07.849 --> 00:08:10.180
OK, I have to roll it.

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:30.400
It’s so bad.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.720
It wouldn’t have mattered though, because
Jigsaw has implemented a safe-check by sending

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:37.470
an electric shock through Adam to ensure that he’s
really dead, which obviously, he isn’t.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:41.510
That’s when the phone that Dr. Gordon found
starts ringing, and it’s his daughter Diana

00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:44.940
telling him that the bad man from her room
is holding them hostage with a gun.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:48.830
The captor also puts Alison on the line, and
she tells him not to believe Adam’s lies.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:49.830
“He knows you.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.300
He knew all about you before today.”

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.220
Let me just make a note of that.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.160
So Gordon finds out the truth about Adam,
that he’s a private photographer hired to

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:05.110
follow Dr. Gordon and gather photos of what
he’s been doing.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:09.120
After revealing these photos, Adam notices
one that he did not take, and asks Gordon

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.880
if somebody else had been at the house.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:14.650
Lawrence determines that it’s Zep, the orderly,
and upon putting a face to his daughter’s

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.560
kidnapper, he really does break down into
a fit of rage.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:20.880
Time expires on the game and another call
comes in on the cell phone, but this time

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:21.880
it’s Alison.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.420
He hears a struggle on the phone, and bursts into tears when he hears

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.910
gunfire and screaming on the other end of
the line.

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:30.630
He sobs on the bathroom floor, where he’s
electrocuted, which may have been Jigsaw giving

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.950
him one more wake up call to spring into action.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:38.810
Dr. Gordon was at rock bottom, and he 👅 had
👅 reached 👅 his 👅 breaking-point.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:42.060
He goes ballistic when the phone rings again
and he’s unable to reach it.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.060
Roll it.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.900
"Noooo!

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:46.960
F*** this s***!

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:47.940
AHHHH!!!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.240
AHHHHHHSDFLJKFSDJKL"

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:50.260
"Lawrence!"

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:53.820
Although he looks crazy, it’s important
to note, that this is what Jigsaw would consider

00:09:53.830 --> 00:09:54.870
to be cured.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:58.180
Because Gordon was being tested for his inability
to feel passion, this…

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.380
"AHHHHHHHHHHH!!!!"

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:00.260
"Lawrence!"

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.440
*laughing* could at least be considered passion.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.040
And that’s enough to motivate him to cave
into Jigsaw’s demands and cut off his own

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.200
foot with the hacksaw.

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:12.060
It would seem that even in this emotional
state, Gordon did not lose his intelligence

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:13.060
and witty thinking.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:16.380
He’s somehow able to communicate to Adam
that he wants to try the “play dead” trick

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.380
one more time.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.760
I’m guessing while we see the back of his
head right here, he winks, and then deliberately

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:21.940
misses the gunshot.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:25.590
This ends up working to his advantage when
Zep arrives at the bathroom to execute him

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:29.540
for failing to win the game before time ran out, because
Adam is able to get in a surprise attack and

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:30.540
disarm Zep.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.770
Gordon goes to get help, and promises Adam
he’ll come back to rescue him.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.600
He crawls away using his one foot, and cauterizes
the wound by burning it on a steaming hot

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:38.100
pipe.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.940
But as he continues to hobble away, he loses
too much blood and is on the verge of passing

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:44.540
out when he encounters an unlikely saviour.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.260
Dr. Lawrence Gordon had basically run out
of strength as he tried to navigate his way

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:59.670
out of the dark corridors beyond the dilapidated
bathroom’s confines, and ended up collapsing

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:00.500
on the floor.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:04.040
After Jigsaw revealed himself to Adam as the
man in the center of the bathroom game, he

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:06.870
made his way out to find Lawrence who had
passed his test.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.600
He drags him to safety and splashes some water
on his face while congratulating him on his

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.240
survival.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:12.820
"Ay congratulations!

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.700
It's a celebration!"

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:18.560
In the coming weeks he nursed Dr. Gordon until
his wound had healed, and gave him a prosthetic

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:19.060
foot.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:23.040
When his health returned to him, he, like
Amanda before him was grateful to Jigsaw for

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:27.390
making him cherish his life once more, and
came on as a disciple and accomplice to Jigsaw’s

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:28.710
work over the next couple years.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:32.880
At some point, Dr. Gordon left the Angel of
Mercy Hospital to go to work at Saint Eustace

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:33.840
Hospital.

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:37.280
I think this change may have been so he could
assist John with testing some of his old co-workers

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.670
at The Angel of Mercy from a safe distance.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.480
Unlike some of his other followers, Jigsaw
saw great potential in Dr. Gordon and kept

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.300
him a secret from the other apostles.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:49.260
Lawrence became Jigsaw’s go-to guy whenever
one of his traps or games required some kind

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:51.350
of surgery or medical expertise.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:55.290
One example of this was in October of 2005
when he helped Jigsaw set up The Death Mask

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:59.000
Trap by using his surgical skills to sew a
key behind the victim’s right eye, which

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.990
he would have to remove in order to escape.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.080
Fans of Saw II noticed early on that the surgeon
seen in the video had a limp, and theorized

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:06.380
it could be Dr. Gordon.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:11.220
In April of 2006, he assisted in the creation
of the Mausoleum trap by sewing shut one man’s

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:14.730
eyes and another man’s mouth, forcing them
to learn a better way to communicate in order

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.220
to avoid being pinched by this powerful mechanism.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:21.000
Not long after, Jigsaw was nearly on his deathbed
while putting together a game that would test

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.960
Amanda Young and a father named Jeff.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.040
"My name Jeff."

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:27.960
Gordon recommends that John also include Jeff’s
wife, Lynn Denlon who had worked under him

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.120
when John was diagnosed at Angel of Mercy.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:33.900
John would have Lynn perform the brain surgery
necessary for her to prove her worth and keep

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.270
John alive long enough to see the end of Jeff’s
trial.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:40.810
After John passed away, Gordon stayed in the
shadows as another Jigsaw disciple, Mark Hoffman,

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:41.840
carried on John’s work.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:45.310
Lawrence demonstrates that he is still devoted
to John’s teachings, even after John’s

00:12:45.310 --> 00:12:49.020
death, by leaving Hoffman a warning when he
starts to stray from Jigsaw’s ideals.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:53.080
He leaves an anonymous note reading “I know
who you are,” in order to try to give Hoffman

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:56.690
a hint that he doesn’t just have free reign
to corrupt Jigsaw’s legacy.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:59.820
Gordon would secretly keep close tabs on Hoffman
from there on out.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:04.020
In July of 2006, he received a parcel through
the mail slot in his door at the hospital.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.590
He opened it to find a video tape with one
final request from John Kramer.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:10.350
He wanted Dr. Gordon to look after his ex-wife
Jill Tuck.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:11.880
“Watch over Jill.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.960
And should anything happens to her,

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.820
I want you to act immediately
on my behalf.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:23.960
In return for that, I will keep no more secrets
from you.”

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:27.600
I don’t know what secrets he thought he
was going to learn with Jigsaw being dead,

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.840
but he’s happy to honor John’s request
anyways.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.740
At some point, Gordon also starts attending
this support group for Jigsaw survivors.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.220
I think he’s mostly there to keep tabs on
the victims that he helped rehabilitate and make

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:40.730
sure they don’t relapse or anything, because
he tends to sit in a chair outside of the

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:43.650
perimeter of the group and seldom participate
himself.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:48.230
That is until one meeting in March of 2007,
when a man named Bobby Dagen attends the group

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:52.330
as part of a press tour for his book, S.U.R.V.I.V.E:
My Story of Overcoming Jigsaw.

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:55.980
Dr. Gordon sees just one issue with this publication.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.890
He knows full well that Bobby Dagen was never
one of the Jigsaw victims.

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:04.160
So he kind of calls him out on it, in what
his probably my favorite scene involving Dr. Gordon.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.520
Let's roll it.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:10.840
[slow clap]
“Remarkable.

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.100
If not a little perverse.

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:19.980
I’m sure I speak for everyone here when
I saw how grateful we are to be part of your…

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:24.220
promotional DVD.”

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.480
That’s hilarious.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:30.010
And I low how the camera operator is like,
‘oh, we gotta get this.’

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.950
And then everyone else starts clapping.

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:32.950
That’s remarkable.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:36.350
But that month, Lawrence continues to keep
a watchful eye over Jill Tuck and of course,

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.350
her enemy, Mark Hoffman.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:41.940
On March 12th 2007, Hoffman is finally able
to catch up with and exact his revenge on

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.860
Jill, which means Gordon is obligated to act
immediately.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:48.690
Hoffman packs a bag of supplies and sets fire
to his safehouse before setting out to make

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:53.050
his escape, but he’s met with three people
in pig masks who are led by Dr. Lawrence Gordon.

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:56.810
It would seem that Gordon has taken a page
from his master and acquired a couple of disciples

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:57.810
of his own.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:01.080
He follows John’s instructions to leave
Hoffman in the location that means the most

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:05.310
to him, the place where he overcame Jigsaw’s
trial: the dilapidated bathroom.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:08.790
But Hoffman is not given the same option that
he had 2 and a half years ago.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.430
He pulls the last remaining hacksaw out of
Hoffman’s reach and throws it out of the

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.960
room, leaving him to die and fulfilling his
teacher’s final request.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.120
"NOOO!"

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:18.220
“Game over.”

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:19.100
"NOOOOO!!!!"

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.990
This would leave Gordon as the only living
true successor to Jigsaw, and that’s the

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:25.510
exciting part about this character.

00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:30.380
In 2016, a forgotten disciple from John Kramer’s
past, a man named Logan Nelson, re-emerges

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.750
and uses the Jigsaw name to get revenge on
a cop that had wronged him and many others.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.740
While this man was trained by Kramer at one
time, he has stayed from his ideals in the

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:40.100
same way that Hoffman did.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:44.130
At the time of recording, we are yet to see
how Dr. Gordon reacts to this, but I imagine,

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:47.640
based on everything that we know about him, that
he’s still keeping a watchful eye and probably

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:51.920
not too happy about Logan Nelson causing his
old master to be dug up from his grave and

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:54.270
having his legacy altered in a negative way
like this.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:57.690
So it will be interesting to see if Dr. Gordon
decides to intervene.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:00.970
John’s intention from the very beginning
with Dr. Gordon was to make him cherish his

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:03.060
life by reintroducing passion.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:06.260
Originally, that is intended to be passion
for his family, Alison and Diana.

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:09.780
It’s never canonically shown what happens
to his wife and daughter, but in an audio

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:13.790
commentary on Saw 7, it’s stated that they
got divorced after Alison saw how Lawrence

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:15.450
had changed following the bathroom game.

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:19.160
There’s nothing in the films to contradict
that, and it does make sense, because they

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:22.480
aren’t present at the support group, but
we can’t say for sure until there some evidence

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:23.480
in a future film.

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:27.680
But what we can say is that passion was reintroduced
into Lawrence’s life anyways, because he

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:31.370
became passionate about Jigsaw’s teachings
and helping people improve their lives using

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:32.370
his methods.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:35.890
This causes him to become the only one of
Jigsaw’s apprentices to become a true heir

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:39.740
to John’s vision of what Jigsaw could be
and it will be fun to see how this new Jigsaw

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:42.470
continues the spirit of John’s teachings
going forward.

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:45.540
Let me know in the comments though, who else
would you like to see covered here on Horror

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:46.360
History?

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.180
I’ve already got a playlist there on the
left of the histories of other Saw characters,

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:53.790
so be sure to check those out and remember
to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:57.180
week, ring that deathbell for notifications
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:59.320
Assuming we both survive.

